> - **Description**: Random forests are an ensemble learning method that constructs multiple decision trees and merges them to improve accuracy and control overfitting.
> - **Strengths**:
>   - **Robust to Overfitting**: Because it averages multiple trees, it can handle high-dimensional spaces well.
>   - **Non-Parametric**: There are no rigid assumptions about the functional form.
