>    plt.xlabel('Input Feature (e.g., Income)')
>    plt.ylabel('Predicted Outcome (Mortality)')
>    plt.legend()
>    plt.show()
>    ```
> 
> ### Conclusion
> 
> Using Gaussian Processes for non-temporal data is a powerful approach. They can seamlessly incorporate uncertainty estimates and adapt flexibly to the structure of your data. With proper kernel selection and careful validation, GPs can provide meaningful predictions even when extrapolating beyond the training data, making them a suitable choice for your modeling needs.
